Description: avfilter/stereo3d: select the correct mono view from interleaved rows
 Keep the configured left row offset for mono-left output and copy the
 right row offset for mono-right output. Swapping offsets only for one
 input order selected the other eye for both irr mono outputs.
 .
 Add a FATE regression that independently generates right-first rows,
 extracts both mono views and joins them in left-first order. It shares
 the analytic reference of the column test and fails before this change.
 .
 Signed-off-by: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
 Assisted-by: gpt-6-astra via Codex
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: other, https://code.ffmpeg.org/danielcamposramos/FFmpeg/commit/e514e07bc9b027d59c1d82d63e340333e34292a2
Forwarded: https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/25377
Last-Update: 2026-11-06

diff --git a/libavfilter/vf_stereo3d.c b/libavfilter/vf_stereo3d.c
index b53eb5a..81eea9e 100644
--- a/libavfilter/vf_stereo3d.c
+++ b/libavfilter/vf_stereo3d.c
@@ -549,16 +549,11 @@ static int config_output(AVFilterLink *outlink)
         s->out.off_lstep = 1;
         break;
     case MONO_R:
-        if (s->in.format != INTERLEAVE_COLS_LR) {
-            s->in.off_left = s->in.off_right;
-            s->in.row_left = s->in.row_right;
-        }
-        if (s->in.format == INTERLEAVE_ROWS_LR)
-            FFSWAP(int, s->in.off_lstep, s->in.off_rstep);
+        s->in.off_left  = s->in.off_right;
+        s->in.row_left  = s->in.row_right;
+        s->in.off_lstep = s->in.off_rstep;
         break;
     case MONO_L:
-        if (s->in.format == INTERLEAVE_ROWS_RL)
-            FFSWAP(int, s->in.off_lstep, s->in.off_rstep);
         break;
     case ALTERNATING_RL:
     case ALTERNATING_LR:
